<title>UK: Zeneca up, Merrill Lynch raises price target.</title>
<headline>Zeneca up, Merrill Lynch raises price target.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Zeneca Plc climbed on Friday as analysts at Merrill Lynch restated a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stock and raised their price target to 19.50 stg from 19.00.</p>
<p>The shares were 22p higher at 17.43 stg by 1008 GMT.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch analyst James Culverwell said the price target has been raised because of positive expectations for three products coming through this year, for treating asthma, migraine and schizophrenia.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
